-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 178  CataTC content port -- Inciting the Elements, Raging Firestorms,
--      Through the Dream
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Companion to the C++ port in src/server/scripts/DC/MountHyjal/zone_mount_hyjal.cpp
-- (section "CataTC content port"). Sourced from
-- `K:/Dark-Chaos/cata stuff/CataTC/src/server/scripts/Kalimdor/zone_mount_hyjal.cpp`,
-- an independent modern-TrinityCore implementation of this zone; the
-- Project-Neltharion source our file was originally ported from never
-- implemented any of it.
--
-- THE HEADLINE FIX: quest 25370 "Inciting the Elements" is currently
-- UNCOMPLETABLE. It requires 4 kills of Twilight Inciter (39926) and 39926 has
-- ZERO spawns -- it is summon-only, reachable solely through the Faerie Dragon
-- chain that was never ported:
--
--     player casts Feed Berries (74513) on a Faerie Dragon (3639921, 64 spawns)
--       -> dragon walks off and forcecasts Spot Infiltrator (74515)
--       -> 74515 FORCE_CASTs 74514 on the PLAYER
--       -> 74514 summons Twilight Inciter (39926), owned by the player so the
--          kill credits their quest
--
-- Also enabled here: 22 already-spawned but completely inert Raging Firestorms
-- (3639939) get their Gout of Flame + Grove Warden defence, and quest 25325
-- "Through the Dream" -- which exists with NO objectives -- gets its Barrow Dens
-- areatrigger completion.
--
-- Apply against acore_world, then restart worldserver (spell_dbc, ScriptNames,
-- areatrigger_scripts and spell_area are all read at startup). Idempotent.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- A) spell_dbc -- 10 spells absent from BOTH the binary Spell.dbc and this
--    overlay table
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Downported from Cata 4.3.4 Spell.dbc + SpellEffect.dbc (build 15601, cached at
-- k:/tmp/cata-dbc/) with Deepholm/tools/spell_downport.py, then widened
-- 232 -> 234 columns exactly as tools/gen_spell_dbc_sql.py does.
--
-- 30991 "Stealth" and 37685 "Backstab" are referenced by the ported AI but are
-- DELIBERATELY NOT INCLUDED: both already exist in the client's binary
-- Spell.dbc (verified against Custom/CSV DBC/Spell.csv), and this fork MERGES
-- the binary file with this table where an overlay row WINS. Adding a
-- downported copy would override two already-correct stock spells for every
-- caster in the game. Only add a row here when the spell is missing from both.
--
-- 75193 and 80550 (the trigger spells of 75192 / 80549) are likewise skipped --
-- already present in this table.
--
-- Chain check: 74515 is a FORCE_CAST (effect 140) of 74514, and 74514 is a
-- SUMMON (effect 28) whose MiscValue is the RAW creature id 39926 -- which is
-- why the script binds Twilight Inciter at 39926 and not at a +3,600,000 clone.
-- 76212's summon MiscValue is likewise the raw 40856.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
DELETE FROM `spell_dbc` WHERE `ID` IN (74513,74514,74515,74565,75192,75206,76205,76212,80549,80576);

